{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall command, and they shall empty the house.</b> The Torah shows concern for the property of Israel, even for earthen vessels. For these vessels regarding which it says ״and they shall empty the house״ and ״and nothing that is in the house shall be declared impure״ — it is speaking of earthen vessels: for if they were immersible vessels (כלי שטף) he immerses them and they are pure; and if there were foods and liquids there, he may eat them during the days of his impurity. This then is certainly speaking only of earthen vessels, because they have no purification in a ritual bath (mikveh)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:20.379715274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}